    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1670">

                <pb facs="1366" n="1250" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11 D 29.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To-day at Cocoa Grove one American civilian killed, three wounded, and seven
                    infantry privates, two marine privates wounded, by Panaman police. Three
                    policemen wounded, one reported killed. Investigation thus far indicates an
                    attack by armed police on unarmed soldiers, for no cause except some altercation
                    among themselves.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
